cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Gravity and the Quantum: Worked Examples"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible worked examples at the gravity-quantum interface, for physics
  students and physicists, with study notebooks and exercises: teleparallel
  gravity (TEGR) and general relativity's classic tests, decoherence and
  complementarity, the entanglement area law, Jacobson's thermodynamic
  argument, and a worked two-diamond design (phase 2.19 rad) for testing
  whether gravity is quantum, as perturbative quantum gravity predicts.
  Bounds on classical-quantum gravity are worked examples within existing
  literature rather than new results. A research note argues that, in 3-3-1
  models, Planck-scale perturbativity selects three colours and three
  generations (conditional; not peer reviewed). Every number is reproduced
  by the scripts in src/.
authors:
